{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' __issue_context__.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"body\": \"### Label\\n\\nreticular pseudodrusen\\n\\n### Synonyms\\n\\nsubretinal drusenoid deposits, SDD, RPD\\n\\n### Synonym type\\n\\nexact (and 2 abbreviations)\\n\\n### Definition\\n\\nSubretinal deposits located internal to the retinal pigment epithelium, composed of aggregations of material in the subretinal space between photoreceptors and the retinal pigment epithelium that can extend through the ellipsoid zone. These deposits have a bluish-white appearance by biomicroscopy and appear as hyperreflective lesions above the retinal pigment epithelium on optical coherence tomography. Reticular pseudodrusen are a strong independent risk factor for late age-related macular degeneration and are particularly associated with geographic atrophy and type 3 neovascularization.\\nPMID:41361163\\nPMID:29859199\\nPMID:38386332\\nPMID:34752962\\n\\n### Parent term\\n\\nMONDO:0006949 retinal drusen\\n\\n### Children term(s)\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### ORCID Identifier\\n\\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\\n\\n### Website URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional comments\\n\\nCrossref: SNOMED:762533006\\nAlthough this terms describes a deposit in the subretinal space, I have chosen the parent term 'retinal drusen' based on the definition, which also makes reference to the subretinal space:\\n> Colloid or hyaline bodies lying beneath the retinal pigment epithelium.\",\n  \"comments\": [],\n  \"title\": \"Request for new term 'reticular pseudodrusen'\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9849\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
